 nuclei with moderate mitotic activity  Immunostains for p63  myosin  calponin  keratin and D 240 confirm the presence of a single focus of invasive carcinoma  rather than DCIS  less than 0 1cm from the deep margin  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO ONE LYMPH NODE  See Table  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  1 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  1  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0  Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  cytokeratin slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    SKIN  RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink soft tissue that is bisected and frozen entirely as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm simple mastectomy with a suture designating the 12 o clock position  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue and posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan white  gritty  ill defined mass that is slightly superior and lateral to the nipple areolar complex  In this area there is a metal clip and packing material  This mass is 1 0cm from the posterior and 1 1cm from the anterior margin  There is focal hemorrhage and cyst formation medial to the mass  The remaining parenchyma is yellow  lobulated  and unremarkable  The axillary region is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area medial to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area lateral to mass  Received fresh  labeled  right mastectomy flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm strip of tan  unremarkable skin  excised to the depth of 0 2cm  The specimen is inked black and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The low grade tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The low grade tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The low grade tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  The high grade tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The high grade tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the high grade tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visual