Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Dennis Sgroi  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lumpectomy with needle loc and x ray  node dissection  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH ASSOCIATED NECROSIS  SEE TABLE  1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Four nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm   See note   GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the lateral  posterior  superior  and posteroinferior margins of the specimen along a broad front   See note   STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  All four tumor nodules are histomorphologically identical  Thus  these nodules most likely represent multifocal disease  The largest nodule demonstrates large areas of necrotic and viable tumor  The tumor seen at the superior margin is necrotic  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  ALL THIRTY TWO  32  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue with one localization wire in place and one localization wire received separately in the specimen container  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked blue  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm solid gray white to soft tan yellow well circumscribed nodule  which abuts the lateral  inferior  and posterior margins and comes to 0 4cm of the superior margin  1 8cm of the anterior margin  and  2 0cm of the medial margin  Abutting and immediately adjacent to this nodule inferiorly is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm solid  firm  gray white nodule  which comes to 1 2cm of the lateral margin  0 9cm of the superior margin  0 7cm of the inferior margin  1 1cm of the posterior margin  2 0cm of the anterior margin  and  2 0cm of the medial margin  Additionally  there is a third firm tan red nodule  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  This nodule is located medial to the two aforementioned nodules and comes to 1 5cm of the dominant nodule  1 0cm of the superior margin  1 6cm of the posterior margin  1 2cm of the anterior margin  and  2 0cm of the inferior  lateral and medial margins  The remaining cut surface displays focally dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well defined solid tan nodule in the medial breast tissue  which is 4 0cm medial to the dominant nodule  2 0cm of the posterior margin  2 0cm of the superior margin  1 7cm of the anterior margin  2 2cm of the inferior margin  2 1cm of the medial margin  and  4 0cm of the lateral margin  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  radial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Dominant nodule  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodules  1 and  2  with nodule  2 entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule  3  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between nodules  3 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary node dissection   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 9cm portion of lymph node bearing tan pink fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning reveals numerous tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two bisected lymph nodes  each   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three bisected lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of