 confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm left breast mastectomy specimen which has an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregular portion of attached axillary tissue  The breast is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm grossly unremarkable white skin  which has a centrally located grossly unremarkable 1 2cm in diameter nipple  The specimen is inked blue at the anterior and black along the posterior aspect  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  indurated  homogeneous  gray white mass in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen  The mass extends to within 0 1cm of the posterior margin and 2 2cm of the anterior margin  The mass is surrounded by abundant dense  gray white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas  The cyst contains clear to brown fluid  Identified 5 0cm medial to the main mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular  slightly indurated  gray white nodule which is in the upper inner quadrant of the specimen and measures 2 2cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated  tan yellow adipose tissue with an abundant amount of interspersed dense  gray white fibrous tissue and focal cystic areas  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  Identified within the axillary fat are multiple firm  tan pink to gray white nodules which may represent lymph nodes  the nodes range from REMOVED_DATE to 3 6cm in greatest dimension  The largest of the nodes is sectioned and has a soft  necrotic cut surface  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of first mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of first mass and nearest to anterior margin and including the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Repr