LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN SEVEN LYMPH NODES  0 7   SEE NOTE   NOTE  All the 7 negative lymph nodes show therapeutic effect  post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Sataloff Grading  N A   No lymphovascular invasion is present  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Nelson  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a 32 x 19 x 9cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is a 32 x 15cm portion of attached skin with a 1 5cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  The skin looks slightly thickened throughout and with a probable 3 4cm in length linear scar located in the lower outer portion of the breast  The anterior margin of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan yellow indurated tumor bed  mass  1   which is located in the upper outer quadrant  0 8cm from the closest posterior resection margin and 3cm from the closest anterior resection margin  Four other masses are identified  There is a 0 6cm nodule  mass  2  adjacent to mass  1  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm tan white nodule  mass  3  that is located 7cm lateral from the larger mass  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm tan white nodule  mass  4  located in the central lower aspect of the breast  10cm away from mass  1 and 7cm away from mass  3  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed tan white firm nodule  mass  5  which is also located in the central lower portion of the breast  19cm from mass  1  14cm from mass  3 and 9cm from mass  4  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and no other masses are identified  Upon examining the axillary tail  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor bed  mass  1  entirely submitted   with the closest posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  2  adjacent to mass  1  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  3  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower outer breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  4  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower inner breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  5   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  5  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper inner breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the skin closest to mass  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the axillary tail tissue  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of yellow tan soft tissue measuring in aggregate 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Seven lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The largest lymph node is indurated with a heterogeneously white  focal yellow and tan brown cut surface  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A trisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 02 54PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor ce