Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  MARY CATHERINE HERTL  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  positive axillary nodes on needle biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Three main nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  1 6cm  and 1 2cm  and multiple additional foci of microinvasion   0 1cm    GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to  0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF THE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on all 3 main nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 IN 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY IN TABLE  2 LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY IN TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  3 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  16 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  SKIN  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are four containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left breast mastectomy specimen which has a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is partially surfaced on the anterior aspect by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of nipple and areolar skin  The nipple measures 1cm in diameter and is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked blue anterior  black posterior  and serially sectioned  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ill defined  indurated  gray white mass in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen which extends to 1 4cm of the posterior margin and 0 4cm of the anterior margin  Surrounding the mass is an abundant amount of dense gray white fibrous tissue  and focal cystic areas  4 2cm medial to the dominant mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular  indurated gray white lesion which extends to 1 4cm of the posterior margin and 2 5cm of the anterior margin  Also identified 1 1cm medial to the second mass and 6cm from the dominant mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined  nodular indurated tan white mass which extends to 0 5cm of the posterior margin and 2 6cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists mostly of dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas consistent with fibrocystic change and lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated and no lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the largest mass to the nearest posterior and anterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue between largest mass and second described mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of second lesion to the nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous tissue between the second lesion and third mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the third mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from masses  Received fresh  labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of multiple irregular tan yellow fragments of adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of lymph node bearing tan yellow portion of adipose tissue which contains multiple possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely as follow  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four possible lymph nodes intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four possible lymph nodes intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible lymph nodes bisected  one inked black  Received fresh  labeled  additional left breast skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular  unoriented portion of white skin excised to a depth of 0 6cm  The epidermal surface is grossly unremarkable  The attached soft tissue is removed and submitted entirely in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  791  to chromosome 17 signals  103  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART D  SKIN  ADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  report_end  , Positive.
