terior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is then serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal fibrous tissue  white and nodular  with firmer areas spanning all quadrants of the specimen and extending to the posterior margin  A well defined mass is not identified  No lymph nodes are identified in the mastectomy specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the middle of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section through the nipple  Received in formalin  and labeled  left axillary contents   is a 7 x 5 x 2 5cm fibrofatty specimen containing candidate lymph nodes  Numerous lymph nodes are identified spanning 1 3cm to 0 2cm  1 candidate large lymph node measuring 3cm in largest dimension is identified as well  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the large lymph node bisected  Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 58 59PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells s