Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  WCP Breast Onc  YAW 9 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  MARGO M MOSKOS  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 43 year old woman with a 2 5cm mass at 2 00 o clock in the left breast which is highly suspicious for breast cancer  A left axillary lymph node was FNA biopsied and sent separately for cytology  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy demonstrate an invasive carcinoma growing in nests and trabeculae with associated desmoplasia  There is a marked  dense associated lymphohistiocytic infiltrate present  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with abundant vacuolated cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with vesicular chromatin and irregular contours  The findings are compatible with a high grade invasive ductal carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   are five cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cas